- [2026-06-25-utinni-table-static-init-race-HANDBACK.md](2026-06-25-utinni-table-static-init-race-HAN
DBACK.md) â€” **DONE 2026-06-25, build-gated, not committed. NO contract change.** Fixed the real 
cause of Utinni's 40/96 ([request](2026-06-25-utinni-table-static-init-race.md)): a static-init read 
race, not a stale exe. The consumer reads `GetEngineHookPoints()` from the injected remote thread 
while main is suspended (pre-`_initterm`); the 29 function-call-initialized rows 
(`pmfToVoid`/`pmfRealEntry`/real-entry accessors) were null then, and MSVC defers the *whole array 
tail* from the first call-row (so even constant rows after it read null). **Fix (Option A):** the 29 
call-rows are now `{name,0}` constant placeholders (whole array image-valid at load), completed by 
`ensureDynamicRowsFilled()` on first call (from `GetEngineHookPoints`/`verifyNoNullNoDup`), on the 
reader's thread. Guarded by a **plain `static bool`** (not a magic-static â€” that would touch the 
uninitialized CRT lock on the pre-resume thread). Pure address arithmetic, idempotent, name-matched 
(all 29 covered, verified). `.h`/`.inc`/version (v5/98)/POD unchanged â†’ no re-sync. Gate: 
Release/Win32 0 unresolved, undecorated `GetEngineHookPoints`, restaged. **Acceptance: re-inject â†’ 
`utinni_init` 40/96 â†’ 96/96.**
