is `#if 0`'d) · `worldSnapshot::wsIsParsePending` (**PURE non-forcing** parse read — the only ws* 
row without a finishLoadNow prologue; lets them WAIT instead of forcing a ~3.1s parse, replacing 
their wsGetNodeCount-as-barrier hack). **RELOAD FIX FIELD-VERIFIED by consumer** (1-2s progressive 
rebuild standing still). **Their reported "NPC regression" is probably NOT ours** — `createObject` 
bails on an existing NetworkId and update()'s delete drain is `isClientCachedOnly`-guarded, so 
neither newly-enabled path can remove server objects; the likely truth is the OBSERVATION PROTOCOL 
changed (pre-fix they had to wander = awareness transition = server re-streams NPCs; post-fix they 
stood still). 10-second falsification test handed over. **Separately flagged, NOT shipped: 
`WorldSnapshot::unload()` deletes by NetworkId with NO isClientCachedOnly guard** (unlike update()'s 
drain) — combined with tatooine's authored SERVER-RANGE ids (≤609,457,649) that can delete live 
server objects; pre-existing, a decision not a patch. **TWO OF OUR OWN ERRORS CORRECTED:** the v27 
ordering RATIONALE was wrong (right conclusion) — `setParentCell` doesn't run the portal sweep, only 
`cellChanged(false)`, which `CellPropertyNamespace::Notification` never overrides; the sweep belongs 
to the TRANSFORM WRITE — comment rewritten; and the "re-sync sha256s byte-identically" checklist 
item was **Utinni-era boilerplate that never applied** (the toolkit doesn't vendor the .h/.inc, they 
bind by name). **OPEN: their `[PortalCullProbe] 1095→exactly 0` after `game::loadScene`** — portal 
traversal apparently not running at all in the editor scene; a hard zero, our domain, next up.
.planning\handoff\README.md:6:- [2026-08-02-toolkit-v26-v27-reload-fix-HANDBACK.md](2026-08-02-toolki
t-v26-v27-reload-fix-HANDBACK.md) — **READ FIRST (latest; pushed `96e20b5aa`).** Contract **v25→v27, 
150 names** in one session plus an engine defect fix. **(1) v26 `game::getShutdownPhase`** — 
process-wide MONOTONIC shutdown signal (0 running/1 requested/2 unwinding), safe from any thread at 
any time; `ExitChain::isRunning()` is UNUSABLE (per-thread `PerThreadData` — a consumer thread 
always reads false) and `game::g_runningFlags`(`&Game::isOver`) goes unsafe exactly when needed. **A 
first cut raised phase 1 only at the `ms_done` sites — window-close goes through 
`!IoWinManager::haveWindow()` and would have logged a bare `0→2`, no early edge on the commonest 
exit path;** caught pre-ship, raise moved after the `while(!isOver())` loop in `Game::run`, then 
**VERIFIED BY MEASUREMENT** on a real `WM_CLOSE` (`[shutdown] phase 0->1`, `1->2`; `CloseMainWindow` 
not `TerminateProcess` — terminating logs nothing and would fake a failure). **(2) LOSSY-RELOAD 
DEFECT FIXED (`04c3f8e11`)** — `WorldSnapshot::loadStep()` had ONE call site outside 
`finishLoadNow()`, inside `GroundScene::updateLoading()` which opens `if (!m_loading) return;` → 
in-world `load()` starts a parse NOTHING pumps while `update()` early-outs on `ms_parsePending` = no 
buildings/collision/creatures; **the toolkit's "returned all at once after moving" was 11 advertised 
rows force-calling `finishLoadNow()`, not movement** — so their buildout-vs-authored ruling-out was 
right for the wrong reason. Pump hoisted into `GroundScene::update` (moved not duplicated). **NOT 
field-verified — consumer must re-test BEFORE rewording their Plan 12/15 checkpoints around a bug 
that may no longer exist.** **(3) v27 `object::setParentCell` (virtual→shim; null cell FATALs via 
`NOT_NULL` so the guard is load-bearing) + `cellProperty::getWorldCellProperty` (out-of-line→plain 
`&fn`, REQUIRED since null can't mean "outside")** — scoped against Kenny's real goal, **placement 
routing** (doorway: place out→`.ws`, in→`.ilf`), not just teleport. Answered their two 
refused-to-guess questions from source: **write o2w never convert** (`attachToObject_w` derives o2p 
from the world frame AND `setTransform_o2w` is itself cell-aware) and **transform FIRST then 
reparent** (`cellChanged` must not observe a stale position). Gates both platforms 0/0, ord-82, 
150==150, boot smoke. Mirrored to SWG-Toolkit. **AWAITING: consumer re-sync + the reload re-test + 
teleport/doorway smoke.**
