**Callers Found**

`WorldSnapshot::unload()` direct callers:

| Call site | Classification |
| --- | --- |
| `src/engine/client/library/clientGame/src/shared/core/WorldSnapshot.cpp:428` in 
`WorldSnapshot::remove()` | Neither requested case: process/ExitChain teardown. Registered at 
`WorldSnapshot.cpp:414` via `ExitChain::add(remove, "WorldSnapshot::remove")`. |
| `src/engine/client/library/clientGame/src/shared/core/WorldSnapshot.cpp:521` inside 
`WorldSnapshot::load(char const *sceneName)` | Inherits from the `load()` caller. It is used for 
both real scene changes and in-place reloads. |
| `src/engine/client/library/clientGame/src/shared/core/WorldSnapshot.cpp:2736` in 
`utinni_wsUnloadSnapshot()` | In-place editor reload. The comment says this is `unload + reset the 
sticky ms_sceneName`; `GroundScene.cpp:2067-2069` explicitly names the editor path as 
`wsUnloadSnapshot + load(getSceneId())`. |

`WorldSnapshot::load()` direct/repo-visible callers:

| Call site | Classification |
| --- | --- |
| `src/engine/client/library/clientGame/src/shared/scene/GroundScene.cpp:1388` in 
`GroundScene::postload()` | Real scene/zone-load path in normal multiplayer. Reached from 
`GameNetwork::startScene()` at `GameNetwork.cpp:480-505`, through `Game::setScene(... 
MultiPlayerSceneCreator ...)` at `Game.cpp:1782-1794`, then `_startScene()` creates the 
`GroundScene` at `Game.cpp:1850-1857`. It can also be reached by the advertised offline/editor 
`game::loadScene` path, but that is not the live-session `wsUnloadSnapshot + load(current)` reload 
case. |
| `src/game/client/application/SwgGodClient/src/BuildoutAreaListView.cpp:101` 
`WorldSnapshot::load("")` | In-place editor reload/live-session style. This is inside 
`BuildoutAreaListView::onEdit()`, after `ServerCommander::editBuildoutArea(areaName)` and 
`WorldSnapshot::setExcludeArea(...)`; it deliberately forces the sticky scene name away. |
| `src/game/client/application/SwgGodClient/src/BuildoutAreaListView.cpp:102` 
`WorldSnapshot::load(Game::getSceneId().c_str())` | In-place editor reload/live-session style. Same 
function, reloads the current scene after the forced empty load. |
| `src/game/client/application/SwgClient/src/win32/engine_advertise.cpp:990` exports 
`"worldSnapshot::load"` as a function pointer | Not a C++ call site, but repo-visible external 
entry. Classification depends on the consumer. In the documented toolkit reload flow it is in-place 
reload when paired with `"worldSnapshot::wsUnloadSnapshot"` exported at `engine_advertise.cpp:1134`. 
|

**Reliable Distinguishing State**

At the `unload()` call site, the only reliable discriminator I found is the call path/symbol itself:

`utinni_wsUnloadSnapshot()` at `WorldSnapshot.cpp:2731-2739` means in-place editor snapshot reload.

Inside `WorldSnapshot::unload()` itself, I did not find reliable state that distinguishes real 
scene/zone change from in-place reload. `GameNetwork::isConnectedToConnectionServer()` / 
`GameNetwork::getConnectionServerConnection()` are reachable symbols (`GameNetwork.cpp:755-758`, 
`GameNetwork.cpp:526-529`), but they do **not** distinguish the two live-session cases: a normal 
multiplayer scene transition and an in-place editor reload can both have a connection server 
session. `ms_sceneName` is also not reliable: `WorldSnapshot::load()` sets `ms_sceneName = 
sceneName` before calling `unload()` at `WorldSnapshot.cpp:520-521`, while 
`utinni_wsUnloadSnapshot()` clears it only after `unload()` returns at `WorldSnapshot.cpp:2736-2737`.

**Cascade Dependency**

Yes, other code depends on container/cell teardown cascade semantics.

The generic owner rule is in `Container::~Container()`: it walks `m_contents` and deletes each live 
object at `Container.cpp:264-275`. `CellProperty` is a `Container` (`CellProperty.cpp:343-344`), so 
cell contents participate in that destructor chain.

Concrete dependencies:

- `World::remove()` depends on containers deleting contained objects: it removes world-list objects 
but skips deleting attached/contained objects because “their container will delete them” at 
`World.cpp:218-226`.
- `WorldSnapshot::utinni_wsRemoveNode()` explicitly documents and relies on the POB/cell cascade: 
the occupancy guard comment says `Container::~Container` cascade-deletes contained objects at 
`WorldSnapshot.cpp:2386-2398`, and the live despawn step says deleting the root cascades through 
cells/contents at `WorldSnapshot.cpp:2458-2460`, then deletes any stragglers at 
`WorldSnapshot.cpp:2460-2468`.

So suppressing the cascade globally would risk leaks or dangling contained objects. I am uncertain 
whether anything depends specifically on deleting **server-owned occupants inside a snapshot POB 
during `WorldSnapshot::unload()`**; I found dependencies on the general container/cell ownership 
cascade, not on that unsafe live-session side effect.
